{"name":"Red Seal","hex":"#c92d21","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"},{"term":"seal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A pinniped (Pinnipedia), particularly an earless seal (true seal) or eared seal."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hunt seals."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Red Seal Program","blocks":[{"text":"Red Seal Program, specifically known as The Interprovincial Standards Red Seal Program, is a program that sets common standards for tradespeople in Canada. It is a partnership between the Canadian federal government, the provinces and the territories."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Red_Seal_Certification_196VI.png/330px-Red_Seal_Certification_196VI.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Seal_Program","wikidata":"Q85851742"},{"title":"Red Seal (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Red Seal is a 1950 Italian crime film directed by Flavio Calzavara and starring Gino Cervi, Carla Del Poggio and Adriano Rimoldi."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/61/Red_Seal_%28film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Seal_(film)","wikidata":"Q7512148"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Red_Seal_Certification_196VI.png/500px-Red_Seal_Certification_196VI.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Red_Seal_Certification_196VI.png/500px-Red_Seal_Certification_196VI.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Specimen of a Red Seal Endorsement (Red Seal number goes where the word \"canoe\" is.)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARed_Seal_Certification_196VI.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/61/Red_Seal_%28film%29.jpg/250px-Red_Seal_%28film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/61/Red_Seal_%28film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/61/Red_Seal_%28film%29.jpg/250px-Red_Seal_%28film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARed_Seal_(film).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%2847